# Serial Communication & Weight Parsing

- The serial manager lives in `apps/desktop/src/serial/serial-manager.ts`. It is constructed with an indicator type plus callbacks for weight and status.
- Indicator types are defined in `apps/desktop/src/parser/index.ts` and map (via factory functions) to BOTH a stream parser and a weight parser.

## Two-stage pipeline

- Stream parsers (`Transform`, e.g. `D300StreamParser`, `LineSplitter`) split raw serial data into lines/frames. They push STRINGS, not objects. They are NOT in object mode.
- Weight parsers (stateful, e.g. `D300WeightParser`, `AveryWeightParser`) receive a string plus a unit and return `WeightReading | null`. They track the last weight to set the `isStable` flag by comparison.

```ts
// stream parser - push a string
this.push(match[1] + 'Wt');

// weight parser - return WeightReading | null
const isStable = this.lastWeight !== null && weight === this.lastWeight;
return { weight, unit, raw: trimmed, isStable };
```

## No hardcoded ports

- Read serial settings from the database row on startup (`settingsRow.serialPort`, `baudRate`, etc.).
- Use the serial manager's `reconnect()` method for live reconfiguration when settings change.
